(1) we can guarantee variables have finite support by treating variable grounding as a graded coeffect.
(2) we can manipulate function return values while preserving finite support using a relevance type system to check point-preserving maps.

Aggregation and weighted logic programming (including bag semantics and semiring provenance) are naturally handled by generalizing from boolean functions to arbitrary pointed output types.

